  "configuration_id": "config_024",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_016: multimodal, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat → 50.7% acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether the multimodal fusion is actually adding value over the image modality alone. The 50.7% accuracy is modest and the F1 (0.455) is notably lower, raising the possibility that the RNA branch is not contributing meaningfully or is introducing noise. config_024 (image_only, multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, transformer) is the closest single-modality counterpart to config_016, sharing the same image encoder, profile setting, and aggregation. Comparing the two will directly tell us whether the RNA encoder (scgpt) and fusion step are helping or hurting. This baseline is essential before committing remaining budget to multimodal optimization; if image-only matches or exceeds 50.7%, the search should pivot toward image-focused configurations, saving experiments from being wasted on multimodal variants that may not outperform a simpler model."
}

